# Architecture & Technical Stack

## Overview
Cambridge Downloader v2 is a hybrid desktop application built using the [Tauri](https://tauri.app) framework. It combines a lightweight web frontend (React) with a performant system backend (Rust).

## 🛠 Tech Stack

### Frontend (User Interface)
- **Framework**: React 18
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Build Tool**: Vite
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS + Framer Motion (Animations)
- **State Management**: React Context + LocalStorage Persistence

### Backend (System Core)
- **Runtime**: Tauri v2 (Rust)
- **HTTP Client**: `reqwest` (with Cookie Store for session persistence)
- **Concurrency**: `tokio` (Async runtime)
- **JSON Parsing**: `serde_json`

## 🏗 Core Design Patterns

### 1. Optimistic Authentication ("Instant Startup")
To eliminate the 8-10 second cold boot time typical of Cambridge servers:
1.  **Frontend**: Checks `localStorage.getItem('session_active')`. If true, it renders the Dashboard *immediately* (0ms delay).
2.  **Background**: Rust asynchronously validates the session via [restore_session](file:///C:/Users/Breeze/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2884cc03-467c-4776-84fa-5822ea174fb9/cambridge-gui/src-tauri/src/commands.rs#84-108).
3.  **Correction**: If validation fails (e.g., session expired), the frontend is signaled to log out.

### 2. Deterministic Caching
Images are cached to disk to prevent re-downloading on every launch.
- **Old Strategy**: Hashed URLs (Failed because Cambridge URLs expire/rotate).
- **New Strategy**: ID-Based. `covers/{book_id}.jpg`.
    - [CoverCacheContext.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Breeze/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2884cc03-467c-4776-84fa-5822ea174fb9/cambridge-gui/src/components/CoverCacheContext.tsx): Manages the frontend memory cache and asks Rust to fetch missing covers.
    - [commands.rs](file:///C:/Users/Breeze/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2884cc03-467c-4776-84fa-5822ea174fb9/cambridge-gui/src-tauri/src/commands.rs): Downloads bytes and writes to the AppCache directory.

### 3. The "App Shell" Model
We treat the [index.html](file:///C:/Users/Breeze/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2884cc03-467c-4776-84fa-5822ea174fb9/cambridge-gui/index.html) as a persistent shell.
- **Login.tsx**: Handles ephemeral identity generation.
- **Dashboard.tsx**: Handles long-running download tasks and library management.
- **TitleBar.tsx**: Custom window controls overlaying the entire app (frameless window).

## 📂 Key Source Files
- [src-tauri/src/commands.rs](file:///C:/Users/Breeze/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2884cc03-467c-4776-84fa-5822ea174fb9/cambridge-gui/src-tauri/src/commands.rs): The main API bridge. All `invoke('cmd')` calls land here.
- [cambridge_downloader_rs/](file:///C:/Users/Breeze/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2884cc03-467c-4776-84fa-5822ea174fb9/cambridge_downloader_rs): A shared Rust library that encapsulates the Cambridge API logic (Login, Search, Download).
- [src/components/ThemeContext.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Breeze/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2884cc03-467c-4776-84fa-5822ea174fb9/cambridge-gui/src/components/ThemeContext.tsx): Handles dynamic theming and randomization.
